  data:  # dd65
    kind: work_item  # dd65
    title: "Publish or close the gap: section 3a can never adjudicate a source that is not inside a walked function (file-anchor + external_symbol = 16.4% of pooled evidence rows)"  # dd65
    status: todo_soft  # dd65
    priority: 2  # dd65
    parent:  # dd65
    tags:  # dd65
    - taint  # dd65
    - adr_0017  # dd65
    - dataflow  # dd65
    - measurement  # dd65
    isbefore: []  # dd65
    duplicate_of: []  # dd65
    not_duplicate_of: []  # dd65
    pr_ref:  # dd65
    description: "ADR-0017 section 3a can never adjudicate a taint flow whose SOURCE is not inside a walked\nfunction. The guard is `fn_has_ddg = source_fn in analyzed`, and `analyzed` / `ddg_symbols` is\npopulated by `build_repo_ddg`, which walks a spec's `function_node_types` and emits only\n`...:function` symbols. Two source-symbol kinds therefore cannot be in it BY CONSTRUCTION:\n\n  - `file` -- the D15 file-kind anchor node, which becomes the \"caller\" when the source is read\n    at MODULE TOP LEVEL, outside any function; and\n  - `external_symbol` -- not a walked in-repo function at all.\n\nBoth come out `analysis_method: structural` no matter how good the extractor is. This is a\nstructural property of an intraprocedural analysis, NOT a per-language wiring gap, and it applies\nto every language equally.\n\nMEASURED, cohort-wide, 2026-08-06 on dev 25ef8937c5. Pooled over the four cohort repos that\nproduce taint findings -- 189 evidence rows:\n\n  source symbol kind    rows    adjudicable by section 3a?\n  function              108     yes\n  method                 50     yes\n  external_symbol        18     NO\n  file                   13     NO\n\n  file-anchor sources          : 13 of 189  ( 6.9%)\n  + external_symbol            : 31 of 189  (16.4%)  structurally un-adjudicable\n\nPer repo the concentration is extremely uneven: express 3/3 (100%), apollo-server 1/1 (100%),\npretix 9/171 (5%), caddy 0/14 (0%). Pooled method split: structural 79, ddg_mixed 105, ddg 5.\n\nFOUND BY the WI-nonad A/B. Wiring JavaScript for DDG moved express from 0 to 154 DDG edges over\n25 symbols, and changed ZERO adjudications, because all four JavaScript findings read\n`process.env` at module top level. Read against source, e.g.\nexpress/examples/cookies/index.js:13:\n\n    if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'test') app.use(logger(':method :url'))\n\nFull A/B: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/WI-nonad-AB.md\n\nWHY THIS IS FILED AS A DISCLOSURE ITEM, NOT A BUG. Nothing here is behaving incorrectly. A\nmodule-scope statement has no enclosing function to build a CFG for, so an intraprocedural walk\nhas nothing to say about it, and `structural` is the honest label. The defect, if any, is that a\nreader cannot currently tell \"the walk ran and did not confirm\" from \"this flow's source is not\nthe kind of thing the walk can ever see\" -- and that distinction is exactly what INV-karud clause\n(a3) exists to protect. `dataflow_coverage` publishes capability per LANGUAGE; it publishes\nnothing about the per-FLOW shapes that are out of scope regardless of language capability.\n\nCANDIDATE RESPONSES, none chosen:\n  (a) Publish the split. Add the un-adjudicable-source-kind counts to `dataflow_coverage` beside\n      the existing per-language rows, so a `structural` label on a file-anchor source is\n      self-explaining. Cheapest, purely additive, no behaviour change.\n  (b) Widen the walk to module scope: treat the file anchor as a synthetic top-level \"function\"\n      and build a CFG over module-level statements. Real work, and it would genuinely adjudicate\n      the express/apollo shape -- module-level config reads are idiomatic in JS and Python.\n      CHECK DIRECTION FIRST: more walks that run means more walks that can return False, and\n      since PR #214 a False plus a same-function sanitizer earns `sanitized`, which DROPS a flow\n      from a claim's violation set. This can SUPPRESS.\n  (c) Nothing, and document the limit in ADR-0017 section 7b beside the other declared exclusions.\n\nMEASURE BEFORE CHOOSING (b): size how many of the 13 file-anchor rows would actually gain a\ndependence, rather than assuming module-scope walks would confirm them. On the express examples\nthe source and sink are 39 lines apart with an `app.listen` callback in between, so the answer is\nnot obviously yes."  # dd65
    fields: {}  # dd65
- op: discuss  # adc0
  at: '2026-08-06T03:48:14Z'  # adc0
  by: agent  # adc0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # adc0
  clock: 2  # adc0
  nonce: adc0  # adc0
  message: "DENOMINATOR CORRECTION on this items own filing, made before it can mislead anyone.\n\nThe description says the 189 evidence rows are pooled over \"the four cohort repos that produce\ntaint findings\". That phrasing asserts the other three produce NONE, and I never measured that.\nWhat actually happened: zoxide, SwiftyJSON and spring-petclinic TIMED OUT on cold analysis during\nthe WI-nonad A/B run and are simply absent from the denominator.\n\nThe adjacent true fact is different and does not license the phrasing: prior cohort work\nestablished those repos produce zero section 3a WALKS. Zero walks is not zero findings — a\nstructural finding needs no walk at all, which is the whole point of this item.\n\nSo read every ratio here as \"of 189 rows across caddy, pretix, express and apollo-server\", not as\na cohort-wide rate. The 16.4% is a four-repo number. Re-running the three missing repos with a\nwarm cache would settle it; until then the denominator is what it is.\n\nThe direction of the error is toward OVERSTATING coverage of the measurement, not the size of the\neffect — the 13 file-anchor and 18 external_symbol counts are exact for the four repos measured."  # adc0
